    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **21 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature on `POST /api/owners`. The household *rejection* rule (Cp10) already existed; this change adds the shared-identifier behaviour (Cp11).\n\n**What the feature does:** when a request sets `sharesHousehold: true` and matches an existing owner with the same last name and address (compared case-insensitively, whitespace-collapsed), the new owner is allowed and receives a stable `householdId`. That same identifier is backfilled onto the existing household member(s), so everyone in the household shares one value, and it's returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` response schema (generates `OwnerDto.householdId`, auto-mapped by MapStruct).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 replaced `householdAlreadyExists(...)` with `findHouseholdMembers(...)`; when a household is matched with `sharesHousehold` true, it assigns a `householdId` to the new owner and backfills existing members. Added `generateHouseholdId(...)`, which derives a deterministic identifier (first 12 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(\"<lastName>|<address>\")` on normalized values) so every joiner in the same household resolves to the same stable value.\n- **Schema SQL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the `household_id` column. hsqldb is the one the tests actually initialize.\n\nThe identifier is deterministic from the normalized household key, which is what makes it \"stable and shared\" \u2014 two independent joiners (B and C in the test) compute the identical value without coordination, and the original owner gets the same value on backfill.",
